# Vivas AI — Agri Input Partner Hub: Antigravity Prompt & SRS

Nov 15, 2026 · @GK

## Summary

Build a new module called **Vivas AgriInput Partner Hub**. Its sidebar label is **Input Partner Hub**, and it sits as a new dropdown directly below **Buy & Procurement** and above **Assets**. It lets seed, fertiliser, urea, nano-fertiliser, bio-stimulant and crop-protection manufacturers host stores, sell to farmers, and see AI-scored field performance of their products, drawn from live Vivas AI field data.

Why that menu position: the Hub feeds purchases into Buy & Procurement and stock into Assets › Materials & Inputs. It also takes its field evidence from Grow › Crop Health, which sits just above in the same sidebar.

Ground rules for Antigravity, applied throughout this doc:

- **Reuse first.** Never recreate a page, table, field or API that already exists. New tables use the `pih_` prefix and point to existing tables by foreign key.
- **Zero change now.** The current app is not touched in phase 1. The few edits it will eventually need are listed separately in *Changes needed in the existing application*, and each needs your approval.
- **Same look.** Follow the existing Vivas AI UI: `index.css` tokens, sidebar `nav-item` / `submenu-item` pattern, lucide-react icons, and the Agro-Intelligence `DESIGN.md`.

## Existing application analysis

The Hub can be built entirely on top of what already exists. I read the `VivasAI` folder (backend `server.js`, `routes/`, `database/*.sql`, `frontend/src`, `DESIGN.md`) on 15 Nov 2026.

**Stack.** React 19 + Vite frontend with lucide-react and Leaflet. Node/Express backend with PostgreSQL (`pg`). Deployed by `deploy.sh` to a Hetzner server behind Nginx + PM2. Navigation is a single `App.jsx` that switches on `currentScreen` (no router). Larger modules are mounted as routers: `/api/ch` (Crop Health), `/api/account`, `/api/settings`.

