**Gaps found that shape the design:**

- No manufacturer / partner entity exists. `vivas_vendors` is per-farm supplier data, so partners need their own tables.
- `vivas_inputs_catalog` has no owner or farm link, so partner products live in a new `pih_products` table and are copied into the farm catalog only when bought.
- `vivas_plantings` is thin (text crop and field names, no `farm_id`). The Hub therefore takes field evidence from `ch_case` and `ch_case_treatment`, which do carry `farm_id`, `crop_id`, `planting_id`, GPS and weather.
- Crop Health diagnosis today is rule-based symptom matching, not an LLM. The Hub AI engine is new, but logs to `ch_ai_request` in the same way.
- Sessions are an in-memory `activeSessions` map, so they reset on restart. A partner portal and an external API need persistent tokens (listed under existing-app changes).
- `vivas_settings_webhooks` and `vivas_settings_api_tokens` are scoped to `farm_id`, so partner keys and webhooks need partner-scoped tables.

