## API specification

There are two route groups: an internal API for the Vivas web app, and a versioned external API for partner systems. Both return `{ success, data, message, meta }`, the same shape the existing routes use.

**Internal API — `/api/pih` (session token, role checked)**

| Area | Endpoints |
| --- | --- |
| Partners | `GET/POST /partners`, `GET/PUT /partners/:id`, `POST /partners/:id/submit`, `POST /partners/:id/review` (approve / reject / suspend + reason), `GET/POST /partners/:id/documents`, `PUT /documents/:id/review` |
| Partner users | `GET/POST /partners/:id/users`, `PUT/DELETE /partner-users/:id` |
| Store | `GET/PUT /stores/:partnerId`, `GET /stores/slug/:slug` (public marketplace view) |
| Products | `GET /products` (filters: crop\_id, problem\_id, type, partner\_id, organic, min\_fps, q, sort, cursor), `GET/POST /products`, `GET/PUT/DELETE /products/:id`, `POST /products/:id/submit`, `POST /products/:id/review`, `POST /products/:id/status`, sub-resources `/skus`, `/composition`, `/suitability`, `/claims`, `/media` |
| Claims review | `GET /claims?sme_status=pending`, `PUT /claims/:id/review` |
| Bulk import | `GET /import/template`, `POST /import` (multipart), `GET /import/:batchId/errors` |
| Outcomes | `GET /outcomes?product_id&farm_id`, `POST /outcomes` (farmer form), `PUT /outcomes/:id`, `POST /outcomes/sync` (admin trigger) |
| Trials | `GET/POST /trials`, `PUT /trials/:id/status`, `POST /trials/:id/observations` |
| Insights | `GET /insights?product_id&crop_id&district&season`, `PUT /insights/:id/review`, `POST /insights/recompute` (admin) |
| Ratings | `GET /products/:id/rating` (overall + per crop + history), `GET /ratings/leaderboard?crop_id&type` |
| Recommendations | `GET /recommendations?farm_id&status`, `POST /recommendations/generate` ({case\_id} or {soil\_test\_id} or {alert\_id}), `PUT /recommendations/:id` (status / dismiss reason), `POST /recommendations/:id/add-to-shopping-list`, `POST /recommendations/:id/create-task` |
| Cart & orders | `GET/POST/PUT/DELETE /cart`, `POST /checkout`, `GET /orders`, `GET /orders/:id`, `PUT /orders/:id/status`, `POST /orders/:id/receive` (creates the inputs lot) |
| Reviews | `GET/POST /products/:id/reviews`, `POST /reviews/:id/reply`, `POST /reviews/:id/flag` |
| Consent | `GET/PUT /consents` (current farm) |
| Partner dashboard | `GET /partner-dashboard/summary`, `/demand-map`, `/fps-trend`, `/sales` |
| Settlements | `GET /settlements`, `POST /settlements/generate` (admin) |
| Keys & webhooks | `GET/POST/DELETE /api-keys`, `GET/POST/PUT/DELETE /webhooks`, `POST /webhooks/:id/test`, `GET /webhooks/:id/deliveries` |

**How the internal API calls existing modules (no duplication)**

- Checkout calls the same service code used by `POST /api/buy/purchase-orders` to create the PO, and by `POST /api/contacts/vendors` to create the vendor if one is missing. Extract shared functions into `services/` only with approval; until then, call the existing endpoints over HTTP internally.
- Receive calls `POST /api/inputs/lots`.
- Create task calls `POST /api/tasks`. Add to shopping list calls `POST /api/buy/shopping-list`.
- Recommendation generation reads `ch_case`, `ch_case_diagnosis` and `GET /api/ch/cases/:id/remedies` for context.

**External partner API — `/api/pih/v1` (header `X-API-Key`, scopes)**

| Method & path | Scope | Purpose |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `GET /v1/products`, `GET /v1/products/:code` | catalog:read | Read own catalogue |
| `PUT /v1/products/:code` | catalog:write | Upsert product (goes to review if composition or claims change) |
| `PATCH /v1/skus/:sku/price`, `PATCH /v1/skus/:sku/stock` | catalog:write | Price and regional stock sync |
| `GET /v1/orders?status&since`, `PATCH /v1/orders/:no/status` | orders | Pull orders, push fulfilment status and invoice |
| `GET /v1/ratings`, `GET /v1/ratings/:code` | insights:read | FPS and badges |
| `GET /v1/insights?product&crop&district&season` | insights:read | Published AI inferences |
| `GET /v1/outcomes/aggregate?product&crop&district` | insights:read | Anonymised aggregates (min 5 farms) |
| `GET /v1/demand?product&district` | insights:read | Open matching field problems by district |
| `GET /v1/docs` | public | OpenAPI 3.1 spec |

Webhook payloads carry `event`, `id`, `created_at` and `data`, with header `X-Vivas-Signature: sha256=<HMAC>`. Retries run at 1 min, 5 min, 30 min, 2 h and 12 h, then the delivery is marked failed and the partner admin is notified.

